    "description": "Khanoumi is an Iranian online retailer centered on beauty, personal care, and related products. Its corporate account describes expansion into business purchasing, industry media, and other services alongside its consumer store.",
    "tags": ["E-commerce", "Beauty retail", "Personal care", "Specialist retail", "Iranian businesses"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "needs_research",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
    "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:55:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-27T18:55:38Z",
    "seo": {
      "title": "Khanoumi: Beauty and Personal-Care E-commerce in Iran | Iran, Unfolded",
      "description": "Explore Khanoumi’s specialist retail model, company-reported development, product information, and published return policies."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "overview",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Specialist retail built around beauty",
        "content": "Khanoumi is an Iranian online retailer associated with cosmetics, skincare, haircare, fragrance, and personal-care products. Its storefront organizes merchandise into detailed categories, including different kinds of cleansers, moisturizers, makeup, and hair products. This structure illustrates the logic of specialist e-commerce: customers need help navigating distinctions within a product field, not simply access to a large undifferentiated catalogue. [s1]\n\nThe website also contains product videos, magazine articles, and selected customer comments. These place editorial and user-generated material beside the shopping journey. Their presence shows how information is incorporated into retail presentation; it does not establish that every product claim or customer account has been independently verified. [s1]",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "development",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "From a specialist store to a broader group",
        "content": "Khanoumi’s corporate timeline dates its website and Instagram activity to Solar Hijri year 1393. It subsequently records investment, the opening of an order-processing center, and expansion into additional business lines. These are company-reported milestones, useful for understanding how Khanoumi describes its development rather than an independently reconstructed corporate history. [s2]\n\nThe same page distinguishes the consumer store from other activities. Khanoumi Bazaar is presented as a business-to-business service connecting wholesale supply and retail purchasing. Khanoumi Business is described as an industry publication, while other divisions concern advertising and brand development. The distinction is practical: a consumer buying skincare, a retailer sourcing stock, and a manufacturer promoting a brand have different relationships with the group. [s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "trust-and-information",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Authenticity claims and product information",
        "content": "In its company profile on LinkedIn, Khanoumi says it sources products from manufacturers or official brand representatives to support authenticity. That statement establishes its declared sourcing approach. It is not an independent certification of every item offered, and this research did not inspect supplier contracts, authorization documents, or product-level testing. [s3]\n\nFor international readers, the important distinction is between a retailer’s assurance, the information supplied about a product, and evidence that independently establishes its origin or performance. Khanoumi’s specialist positioning makes those questions central to understanding the business. Claims that it is the first or largest retailer in its field are not adopted here because a dated, independently supported comparison was not established. [s3]",
        "source_ids": ["s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "returns",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Why product categories affect returns",
        "content": "Khanoumi’s published return FAQ distinguishes concerns about authenticity, changes of mind, electrical products, and gold. For ordinary changes of mind, its answers emphasize original condition and intact seals. The page also directs customers to coordinate a return with support before sending goods back. These provisions show why a simple promise of returns needs to be read alongside category-specific conditions. [s4]\n\nThe wording is not entirely uniform: one answer stresses hygiene restrictions, while another describes returns for sealed goods in their original condition. This page therefore does not reduce the policy to an unconditional guarantee. The FAQ is evidence of the retailer’s published position when inspected, not a legal assessment or proof of how every complaint is handled. [s4]",
        "source_ids": ["s4"]
      },
      {
        "id": "significance",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "What Khanoumi illustrates",
        "content": "Khanoumi offers a focused example of commerce organized around a product field, with consumer shopping connected to content and adjacent industry services. Its corporate descriptions suggest a business seeking relationships across supply, promotion, and consumption. Evaluating the results requires more than a catalogue or a milestone timeline: comparable annual operating data and independent evidence of customer and supplier outcomes remain necessary. [s1][s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      }
    ],
